description: 'Design+implement the declarative config-block construct so project.jn
  parses via the real Jinn parser (docs/lamp-prereqs.md §4, lamp.md §2/§2.1) instead
  of a bespoke pkg.rs reader. An indentation-scoped block of `key is <literal|list|nested-block>`
  plus a whitelisted set of declarative connector keywords (requires, from, git, rev,
  opt, with, enables). Pin the exact grammar incl. multi-setting lines (`release is
  opt 3, debug-info false`) and clause lists (`postgres is requires ext/pq, enables
  ''metrics''`) without colliding with expression-statement parsing (Q3). Restriction
  enforcement (§2.1: no calls, no control flow, no *name defs) as a validation/lint
  pass yielding precise diagnostics. Make construct general but initially wire only
  the manifest schema; document provisional status in docs/stability.md. Independent
  of 2-32-1..4 — can proceed in parallel. Definition of done: the full lamp.md §2
  example manifest parses+validates with precise errors on violations; tests pin the
  grammar.'
